2
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Coolant piping, routed above a live
power feeder.

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Kirchhoff caught it, cited the
tender clause, and fixed it.

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:13,000
This is Kirchhoff.
AI designs. Physics checks.

5
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:16,000
An engineer signs.

6
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:21,000
AI halls need power and liquid
cooling designed together.

7
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:26,000
And engineers check AI by hand: only
6 percent trust its results unverified.

8
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Drop in the tender. Gemini
reads it, and a requirement

9
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:34,000
only counts if its quote is
found on the cited page.

10
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Intake even catches the client
contradicting itself.

11
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:42,000
The engineer approves the plan.

12
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:46,000
Agents place 48 racks at
132 kilowatts each.

13
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:50,500
Power and Cooling work in
parallel: a 2N electrical

14
00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:55,000
system and nine 1.2-megawatt
CDUs.

15
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Then the checker runs. It's
deterministic, with no LLM

16
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:05,000
in the verdict path, so the
AI can't mark its own homework.

17
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:10,000
149 checks: 147 pass, two
fail, each citing its clause.

18
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:15,000
Feeder FA-01 drops 2.16 percent
against a 2 percent limit.

19
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:19,000
Every fix is re-checked against
every rule before an agent

20
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:23,000
may pick it.

21
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:27,000
It checks the supply chain too.

22
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:31,000
The 2.5 MVA transformer has a
98-week lead time; the tender

23
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:35,000
allows 26. Kirchhoff swaps to a
3.15 MVA unit in stock,

24
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:40,000
and re-checks the fault level.

25
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:43,000
(In-clip) What if racks go to
200 kilowatts?

26
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:47,000
The engine re-runs every rule
in about 8 milliseconds.

27
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:51,500
18 impact chains light up across
power and cooling:

28
00:01:51,500 --> 00:01:56,000
transformers at 113.6 percent,
cooling zones over capacity.

29
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:00,000
Nothing ships until an
engineer signs.

30
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:04,000
The review shows the diff and
every assumption, then stamps

31
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:08,000
the revision hash. Approval
raises purchase requisitions

32
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:12,000
in the ERP and moves the CRM deal.

33
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:15,500
Engineering, procurement and

34
00:02:15,500 --> 00:02:19,000
sales, in one workflow.

35
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:23,000
Same engine, new asset packs:
a 132 kV grid line,

36
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:27,000
and a five-megawatt-peak
solar field.

37
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:32,000
It caught all 35 seeded design
faults, with zero false positives.

38
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:37,000
Built on Gemini, ADK, Cloud Run,
Firestore and Firebase.

39
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:41,000
Kirchhoff, by team Ordinal,
for the future of work.

40
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:45,000
Try it at kirchhoff dot
web dot app.
